WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.419 --> 00:00:06.040
Film Courage: So Alberto writes in “Can
the main character have two desires?”

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:11.790
Peter Russell, Screenwriter/Story Consultant:
Sure…but usually only one wound.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:18.670
People often think…they get excited about
the core wound which they should because it

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.789
really gives you an original character.

00:00:20.789 --> 00:00:24.510
And we in real life we have a dozen wounds,
right?

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.830
Let’s talk about mine or not.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.820
But everybody has more than one wound.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:35.120
But movies and to some extend television,
they are simple okay?

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.879
So you want to sort of see one big wound.

00:00:39.879 --> 00:00:45.289
Big then many desires come out of that.

00:00:45.289 --> 00:00:49.679
Tony Soprano had one big wound - my mommy
hates me.

00:00:49.679 --> 00:00:55.920
But a bunch of desires came out of that - I
love bad girls, I love working at a club,

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:03.429
I love hurting people, I love to be mean,
I love to run things, I love being a boss,

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:06.020
I love being a dad.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.000
So you can have many desires.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.940
Just know that all of the desires come out
of the wound and they are often unhealthy

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:18.359
okay, that’s what we want to see.

00:01:18.359 --> 00:01:22.750
If they were healthy, there would be no show.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:28.210
Especially in television, you get wounded
and then you do a lot of unhealthy things

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:34.420
and sometimes your superpower and in television
that’s another thing you need to know.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:37.700
Usually in television the hero has a superpower.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:42.520
And usually that superpower (especially at
the beginning) can be used for wrong reasons

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.400
(bad purposes).

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:50.119
For instance, Don Draper in MADMEN has a superpower,
he’s insanely seductive.

00:01:50.119 --> 00:01:55.780
And he’s seductive as a womanizer and he’s
seductive as an ad man.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:59.060
But it comes from the fact that his mommy
didn’t love him, right?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:01.249
He feels unloveable.

00:02:01.249 --> 00:02:08.160
So all the things he does, he uses his superpower
for bad reasons because he’s wounded.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.220
He seduces women, right?

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:18.670
He does ad campaigns for cigarettes and horrible
things and he’s immoral as an ad man because

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:20.620
he is misusing the superpower.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:23.390
But the superpower came from his wound.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:29.030
He he hadn’t been wounded (I’m not lovable)
he would never have become a great seducer,

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:30.510
he wouldn’t have needed to.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:35.890
So the superpower is related to the wound.

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:44.680
But the things we wants come out of the unhealthy
desires of him trying to make the wound go

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.680
away.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.910
Trying to feel better about the wound.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:03:00.269
Every desire is an attempt to sopophorize
the wound, to palliate the wound.

